Both Oracle and IBM are providing all their results and documentation to the
community by way of the CommonCriteria Evaluated Linux Consortium (CCeLinux
Consortium).

We are re-working The Center of Open Source & Government site [egovos.org]
to have information on the CCeLinux Consortium with a mailing list, so you
can ask questions of the people working on this at Oracle and IBM. That site
re-work should be ready by the Open Source in Government Conference in Paris
in November.

Best regards,
Tony

